  "statement": "Let \\(a, b, c, n\\) be positive real numbers such that \\(\\frac{a+b}{a}=3, \\frac{b+c}{b}=4\\), and \\(\\frac{c+a}{c}=n\\). Find \\(n\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2018-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Answer: \\(\\frac{7}{6}\\)\nWe have\n\n\\[1=\\frac{b}{a} \\cdot \\frac{c}{b} \\cdot \\frac{a}{c}=(3-1)(4-1)(n-1) .\\]\n\nSolving for \\(n\\) yields \\(n=\\frac{7}{6}\\).",
